  SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

  QuickShare — declares Chattr chats as share targets, so recent conversations
  can appear in the Direct Share row at the top of the system share sheet.

  This file holds NO shortcuts. The conversations themselves are published at
  runtime by ShareSuggestionsChannel.kt as long-lived dynamic shortcuts; what a
  <share-target> does is tell the system which of those shortcuts may be offered
  as a share destination, and for which content.

  The <category> below is the join: it must match SHARE_TARGET_CATEGORY in
  ShareSuggestionsChannel.kt exactly. A mismatch fails silently — the shortcuts
  exist, the row simply stays empty.
-->
<shortcuts xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <!-- Mirrors MainActivity's ACTION_SEND intent filter in AndroidManifest.xml;
         keep the mime types in sync with it, or a type will be shareable to the
         app but not to a person. -->
    <share-target android:targetClass="net.geraldhofbauer.chattr.MainActivity">
        <data android:mimeType="text/plain"/>
        <data android:mimeType="image/*"/>
        <data android:mimeType="video/*"/>
        <data android:mimeType="audio/*"/>
        <data android:mimeType="application/*"/>
        <category android:name="net.geraldhofbauer.chattr.dynamic_share_target"/>
    </share-target>
</shortcuts>
